assertion  XSH.ctan.006
anchor     functions/ctan.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       For ctan, in the page's notation w stands for the product i*z, and
           the value given is the factor that -i multiplies; the call is on z
           = -i*w (parts exchanged, one sign changed) and the result is -i
           times that factor. w = +Inf + iy (y positive finite) gives 1 + i0
           sin(2y): real part 1 and a zero imaginary part with the sign of
           sin(2y) (y = 1 gives +0, y = 2 gives -0).
note       The tag on this passage is the IEC 60559 Complex Floating-Point
           option; the test is NOTINUSE unless the C implementation claims it
           (Annex G of the C standard). No error is defined on this page, so
           errno is not examined; an exception is checked only when
           math_errhandling includes MATH_ERREXCEPT. The page states the cases
           in terms of the product iz and of -i times the result, without
           defining them; the test reads them as the exact exchange of the
           parts with one sign change (a formal product would turn an infinite
           part into NaN). See Q-112.
test       t/006-plus-inf-finite.c

